# REFERENCE

## Cold start

- What this is: sagdi.com rebuilt as a public "hub", branch `rewamp2026` of this repo
  (`sagdi-portfolio/`, Next.js 15 App Router, Tailwind v4, next-intl en·ru·uz). `main` is the old
  site and is what's live. The branch replaces it at step 7.
- Run: `npm run dev` from this folder. `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build` must
  stay green.
- How Sagdi works: plain English, answer first, short. Build the literal ask and stop; ask one plain
  question when something is ambiguous. Verify in the running app before saying done, and label
  anything you couldn't run UNVERIFIED. No em dashes in any user-visible copy. He often keeps this
  file open in vim.
- Keep this file current: tick boxes, move sections between IN PROGRESS / NEXT / DONE, never delete.

## Environment variables

- Local: `.env.local` (gitignored) has the photo variables. Whether the Notion and Resend keys are in
  it locally is unchecked. Compare against `env.local.template`.
- Vercel: `PHOTOS_BASE_URL`, Notion and Resend keys are all set for All Environments.
- Any variable added or changed in Vercel needs a redeploy. The home page is built statically and
  refreshes hourly, so it only sees new variables on the next build.
- Notion: `NOTION_API_KEY`, `NOTION_DATABASE_ID`, optional `NOTION_DATA_SOURCE_ID`. The database needs
  these properties: Title or Name (title), Slug (rich text), Tags (multi-select), Published
  (checkbox), Published Date or Date (date), Description (rich text). It must be shared with the
  integration in Notion.
- Resend: `RESEND_API_KEY`, `CONTACT_TO_EMAIL`, `CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL`.
- Photos: `PHOTOS_BASE_URL` (the site) + `R2_ACCOUNT_ID` (32-hex only), `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`,
  `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `R2_BUCKET` (sync script only, local). `next.config.ts` parses
  `PHOTOS_BASE_URL` at build time: a value without `https://` breaks the build.

## Photos: how it works

- Bucket: Cloudflare R2 `sagdi-photos`, public URL `https://pub-d80e4e9eb39747c9b6eeca7668d027ed.r2.dev`.
- Sets are folders: `photos-src/<set>/` on Sagdi's machine (gitignored). `home/` is the home strip.
  A new photo block anywhere is a new folder plus `listPhotos("<set>")`.
- Day to day, order/add/delete happen in the PHOTO MANAGER, not by hand: double-click
  `photo-manager/Open Photo Manager.command` (or `node photo-manager/server.mjs`). It opens
  http://127.0.0.1:4455, shows the set in publish order, and does drag-to-reorder, drop-to-add
  (HEIC → JPEG via `sips`, non-H.264 video → mp4 via `avconvert`), ✕ to `photos-src/.trash/<set>/`,
  caption/alt boxes, a Loop checkbox per video, Publish and "Check the site". The folder is
  gitignored, so it never reaches Vercel. How to use it: `photo-manager/README.md`.
- Order lives in `set.json`, which the manager writes:
  `{ "order": "newest-first" | "oldest-first", "sequence": ["<file>", …],
     "items": { "<file>": { "alt", "caption", "loop": false } } }`. `loop` is written only when
  off; videos loop by default.
  `sequence` is the exact order; files missing from it join at the newest end (front for
  newest-first, which home is). With no `sequence` it's the old rule — by filename, reversed for
  newest-first — where a `010-` prefix sorts LAST in a newest-first set, not first. All alt text is
  empty right now.
- Sync: `npm run photos:sync -- [<set>…]` (Publish runs the same script). Uploads per photo a
  720px-tall WebP (what the strip shows), full-view WebPs at 1600 and 2560px on the longest side
  (skipped when bigger than the photo) and the 3000px JPEG original; videos as-is. All named by
  content hash and cached immutable.
  Anything already in the bucket is reused straight from the published manifest — not re-encoded —
  so a reorder finishes in seconds. One manifest per set at `photos/<set>/manifest.json`, written
  last so a half-finished run changes nothing. Hidden files (`._x.jpg`), `.heic` and same-content
  twins are skipped with a warning. A lock file stops two runs at once.
- Deleting happens in the same run: once the new manifest is up, every bucket file in that set the
  manifest doesn't name is removed. Safe because the site re-reads the manifest every 60s and the
  strip drops a frame whose file is gone. (The old separate `--cleanup` step no longer exists.)
- The carousel loads the WebP straight from R2 (`unoptimized`). Next's image optimizer is left out on
  purpose: it gives up on a fetch after 7s, and on a home connection that showed as broken frames.
- Videos play muted while at least 60% of the frame is inside the strip and the strip is on
  screen; a play-once video plays once each time it comes into view. Videos must be H.264 mp4: iPhone HEVC plays in Chrome on a Mac but not in Firefox or on
  some phones, so the manager converts anything that isn't H.264 mp4 when you add it.
- Full-screen view (`src/components/ui/photo-viewer.tsx`): tap a strip photo. It loads the
  smallest full-view WebP at least as wide as the photo will be on that screen, only for the
  open photo and its neighbours, showing the strip WebP until it arrives. Back closes it (it adds
  one history entry on open).
- If frames show as samples on a deploy: `PHOTOS_BASE_URL` wasn't there at build time. Redeploy.
- Left as is, by choice: r2.dev is rate-limited and not edge-cached. A custom domain
  (`photos.sagdi.com`) needs sagdi.com's DNS on Cloudflare.
